*Experiment 6(a) - Write a shell script that determines the period for which a specified user is working on the system*

*Steps*
1) Open the ubuntu terminal
2) Create a shell script -> nano http://user.sh
3) Enter the required shell script to check the specified user's login / working time
4) Save and Exit the file -> Ctrl+O, Enter & Ctrl+X
5) Give execution permission -> chmod +x http://user.sh
6) Execute the script by passing the username (./user.sh xbox user)
7) The script displays the user's login time if the user is currently logged in

*Script used:*
#!/bin/bash
read -p "Enter username: " user
login_time=$(who | awk -v u="$user" '$1 == u {print $3, $4; exit}')
if [ -z "$login_time" ]
then
  echo "user is not currently logged in."
else
  echo "Login time: $login_time"
fi
*Result:* Successfully determined the login / working period information of the specified user
